{"title":"Features of Adulthood","link":"https://kottke.org/25/01/features-of-adulthood","date":1736279321000,"content":"\n        <p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/xkcd-adulthood.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/xkcd-adulthood.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/xkcd-adulthood.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"1144\" alt=\"the features of adulthood graphed by how often they come up vs how often I expected them to come up\" /></p>\n\n<p>I enjoyed Randall Munroe’s take on what he thought adult life would be like as a kid…<a href=\"https://xkcd.com/3034/\">in the form of a graph</a>, naturally. All those Looney Tunes reruns &amp; 80s movies led us Gen Xers astray.</p>\n\n        \n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/infoviz\">infoviz</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Randall%20Munroe\">Randall Munroe</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/XKCD\">XKCD</a></p>\n\n         <p>💬 <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/01/features-of-adulthood\">Join the discussion on kottke.org</a> →</p>\n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"92e06f7816d284becf47db36a6bf32813cd18982a3e814d716e6579c9bcb3f7d","category":"Sites"}